    <briefdescription>
<para>Signed shard-to-shard request payload. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Signed Request Protocol</para>
<para>Provides defense-in-depth security layer on top of mTLS. Requests are signed with the sender&apos;s private key and include:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Timestamp for freshness validation</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Nonce for replay protection</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Certificate serial for identity verification</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>This protects against:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Replay attacks</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Man-in-the-middle (additional layer beyond mTLS)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Request tampering </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
